ing review lease for Ready tasks[/bold #D7AFFF]\n[dim]   Goal: [#D7D7AF][/dim]Every visible, non-recurring Ready task can carry a human-confirmed[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]\\[fresh:: YYYY-MM-DD]. A task that was never confirmed (every new [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]capture) or was confirmed longer ago than its refresh interval is [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]due for review. The interval is 7 days by default and can be [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]overridden per task, per note, and in config. Bryan works through [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]the due tasks each morning in their source notes with ]s / [s and [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]Alt+F / Alt+Shift+F, and the status bar always shows how many tasks[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]are due and how many he refreshed today. Every supported keymap and[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]bob capture edit stamps the tasks it rewrites; task creation and [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]automation never do.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim] Counts: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]10[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] phases[dim][/dim] · [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]7[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] waves[/dim]\n[dim]   Path: [#87AFFF][/dim]plan:202609/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]task_freshness_review.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim] Prompt: [#87AFFF][/dim]prompts/202609/task_freshness_review.md[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Bead: [#87AFFF][/dim]bob-cli-31[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Page: [#87AFFF][/dim]https://github.com/bobs-org/bob-cli--beads/blob/main/pages/bob-cli-31/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]README.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Freshness contract, placement helper, evaluator, and config in[bold black on #FFD75F][/bold #D7AFFF] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]bob-cli[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]fresh-core[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]fresh-core: docs/freshness.md (definition, placement and state rules, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]conformance vectors), the Rust placement helper stamp_fresh / [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]set_refresh, the pure evaluator, and the freshness: config block, with a[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]test per vector and parse-invariance tests for both Rust task parsers.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]bob freshness list and seed[/bold #D7AFFF]                                   [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]fresh-cli[dim] · [dim][/dim]after fresh-core[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]fresh-cli: headless review queue (bob freshness list, human and JSON) [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]and a guarded, idempotent, staggered cutover seed (bob freshness seed) [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]that aborts on any parse change, plus help, README, and CLI tests.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]bob capture stamps the existing tasks it rewrites[/bold #D7AFFF]             [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]capture-stamps[dim] · [dim][/dim]after fresh-core[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]capture-stamps: plan_task_link and the =x in-progress close stamp fresh [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]in the same write; creation never stamps; hooks preserve the field; docs[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]and tests updated.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Seed the live vault and mute the fields[/bold #D7AFFF]                       [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]seed[dim] · [dim][/dim]after fresh-cli[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]seed: install bob from master, dry-run then apply bob freshness seed to [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]~/bob, verify that no task parses differently before and after, add the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]CSS rule that mutes fresh and refresh, and vault-sync.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  5 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]bob-ledger-tools api v3 freshness namespace and status bar[/bold #D7AFFF]    [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]ledger-freshness[dim] · [dim][/dim]after fresh-core, seed[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]ledger-freshness: the JavaScript evaluator and placement helper on the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]shared vectors, api v3 (api.freshness with stampLine, state, isDue, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]tier, rank, queue, counts), the freshness: config, and a status bar [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]counter that clicks through to the next due task.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  6 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Review keys in Bob Navigation Hotkeys[/bold #D7AFFF]                         [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]nav-review[dim] · [dim][/dim]after ledger-freshness[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]nav-review: vault-wide next/previous due-task jumps (Ctrl+Alt+J/K, and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]the commands behind ]s / [s), Alt+F refresh with no other change, and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]Alt+Shift+F refresh-and-advance, including counted and Task Link modes.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  7 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Bob Navigation Hotkeys gestures stamp freshness; Ctrl+Shift+P [bold black on #FFD75F][/bold #D7AFFF] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]refresh row[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]nav-stamps[dim] · [dim][/dim]after nav-review[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]nav-stamps: Alt+N, the Ctrl+Shift+P property/lane rows, Ctrl+Shift+M [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]moves, and the dependency toggle stamp every open task they rewrite, and[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]a new pinned refresh row sets or clears \\[refresh:: N].[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  8 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Status cycling and Task Link gestures stamp freshness[/bold #D7AFFF]         [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]cycler-link-stamps[dim] · [dim][/dim]after ledger-freshness[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]cycler-link-stamps: task-status-cycler (Alt+[ / Alt+] to an open status,[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]leaving Blocked, reopening) and block-id-prompt (Ctrl+Shift+Enter and ^^[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]when they rewrite the task line) stamp through api.freshness.stampLine.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  9 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Review note, dash chip, vim maps, chores, and config[/bold #D7AFFF]          [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]vault-review[dim] · [dim][/dim]after nav-review, seed[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]vault-review: freshness.md review note, a REVIEW dash chip, ]s / [s [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]vimrc maps, the Morning review and Weekly prune chore text, and the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]freshness: block in the chezmoi-managed config.yml.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  10 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Install, end-to-end check, glossary term, and Bryan's [/bold #D7AFFF]       [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n       [bold #D7AFFF]checklist[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]rollout[dim] · [dim][/dim]after capture-stamps, nav-stamps, cycler-link-stamps, [/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#AF87FF][dim]vault-review[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]rollout: install bob and confirm plugin deploys, run the headless [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]end-to-end checks, add the Task Freshness glossary strand, finalize the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]docs Surfaces table, and hand Bryan his visual checklist and tuning [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]steps.[/#D7D7AF]","clan_tribe":"epic","epic_bead_id":"bob-cli-31","llm_provider":"muse","model":"muse-spark-1.3-contributor","patch_name":"gh_bobs-org__bob-cli","phase_bead_id":"bob-cli-31.1","reasoning_effort":"xhigh","vcs_provider":"GitHub"},"source_run_id":"run-35ef9ee94f81137934dafb5f6f46f5d9","started_at":"2026-09-30T23:32:44.030940+00:00","state":"active"},{"capabilities":{"durably_revivable":true,"historically_viewable":true,"missing_requirements":[],"restartable":true},"commits":[{"committed_at":1790814232,"sha":"